===Noun===
{{en-noun|feet|foot|pl2qual=UK colloquial, unit of measure}}

# A biological structure found in many [[animal]]s that is used for [[locomotion]] and that is frequently a separate [[organ]] at the terminal part of the [[leg]].
#: {{ux|en|A spider has eight '''feet'''.}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Specifically, a [[human]] foot, which is found below the [[ankle]] and is used for [[stand]]ing and [[walk]]ing.
#: {{ux|en|Southern Italy is shaped like a '''foot'''.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Revelation|1|17|passage=And when I ſawe him, I fell at his '''feete''' as dead : and hee laid his right hand vpon me, ſaying vnto mee, Feare not, *I am the firſt,and the laſt.}}
# {{lb|en|often used attributively}} Travel by [[walking]].
#: {{ux|en|We went there by '''foot''' because we could not afford a taxi.}}
#: {{ux|en|There is a lot of '''foot''' traffic on this street.}}
# The [[base]] or [[bottom]] of anything.
#: {{ux|en|I'll meet you at the '''foot''' of the stairs.}}
# The part of a [[flat]] surface on which the feet customarily rest.
#: {{ux|en|We came and stood at the '''foot''' of the bed.}}
# The end of a rectangular [[table]] opposite the [[head]].
#: {{ux|en|The host should sit at the '''foot''' of the table.}}
# A short foot-like [[projection]] on the bottom of an object to support it.
#: {{ux|en|The '''feet''' of the stove hold it a safe distance above the floor.}}
# {{senseid|en|unit}} A [[unit of measure]] equal to twelve [[inch]]es or one [[third]] of a [[yard]], equal to exactly 30.48 [[centimetre]]s.
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=XX|passage=No. I only opened the door a '''foot''' and put my head in. The street lamps shine into that room. I could see him. He was all right. Sleeping like a great grampus. Poor, poor chap.}}
#: {{ux|en|The flag pole, which is 20 '''feet''' high, was hoisted by a six-'''foot''' tall man.}}
#: {{ux|en|My sis's just over six '''foot''' two.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{ellipsis of|en|[[square]] foot}} {{ng|A unit of {{l|en|area}}.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{ellipsis of|en|[[cubic]] foot}} {{ng|A unit of {{l|en|volume}}.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A unit of measure for [[organ]] [[pipe]]s equal to the [[wavelength]] of two [[octave]]s above [[middle C]], approximately 328 mm.
# {{lb|en|collective|military}} Foot soldiers; [[infantry]].
#: {{ux|en|King John went to battle with ten thousand '''foot''' and one thousand horse.}}
#* {{RQ:Clarendon History|passage=His forces, after all the high discourses, amounted really but to eighteen hundred '''foot'''.}}
# {{lb|en|cigars}} The end of a [[cigar]] which is lit, and usually cut before lighting.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|author={{w|Jonathan Escoffery}}|title={{w|If I Survive You}}|publisher=4th Estate (2023)|page=128|passage=He removes a gold lighter from his pocket, flips it open, and waves the flame over the '''foot''', taking short, sucking pulls off the head till it’s lit.}}
# {{lb|en|sewing}} The part of a [[sewing machine]] which presses downward on the fabric, and may also serve to move it forward.
# {{senseid|en|printing: bottommost part of a page}} {{lb|en|printing}} The bottommost part of a [[type]]d or [[print]]ed page.
# {{lb|en|printing}} The base of a piece of type, forming the sides of the [[groove]].
# {{lb|en|prosody}} The basic measure of [[rhythm]] in a [[poem]].
# {{lb|en|phonology}} The parsing of syllables into [[prosodic]] [[constituent]]s, which are used to determine the placement of [[stress]] in languages along with the notions of constituent [[head]]s.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The bottom edge of a [[sail]].
#: {{ux|en|To make the mainsail fuller in shape, the outhaul is eased to reduce the tension on the '''foot''' of the sail.}}
# {{lb|en|billiards}} The end of a billiard or pool table behind the foot point where the balls are [[rack]]ed.
# {{lb|en|botany}} In a [[bryophyte]], that portion of a [[sporophyte]] which remains embedded within and attached to the parent [[gametophyte]] plant.
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=4|text=(''b'') sporophyte with '''foot''' reduced, the entire sporophyte enveloped by the calyptra, which is ± stipitate at the base.}}
# {{lb|en|malacology}} The muscular part of a [[bivalve]] [[mollusc]] or a [[gastropod]] by which it moves or holds its position on a surface.
# {{lb|en|molecular biology}} The globular lower [[domain]] of a [[protein]].
# {{lb|en|geometry}} The point of intersection of one line with another that is perpendicular to it.
# Fundamental principle; basis; plan.
#* {{RQ:Berkeley Alciphron|volume=II|section=XXXI|page=121|passage=To conſider the vvhole of the Subject, to read and think on all ſides, to object plainly, and anſvver directly, upon the '''foot''' of dry Reaſon and Argument, vvou'd be a very tedious and troubleſome Affair.}}
# Recognized condition; rank; [[footing]].
#* '''May 20, 1742''', {{w|Horace Walpole}}, ''letter to Horace Mann''
#*: As to his being on the '''foot''' of a servant.

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|unit of length}}
** The ordinary plural of the unit of measurement is {{m|en|feet}}, but in some contexts, {{m|en||foot}} itself may be used ("he is six foot two"). This is a reflex of the Anglo-Saxon (Old English) genitive plural.<ref name="aue-faq">Rich Alderson, “Why do we say ‘30 years old’, but ‘a 30-year-old man’?”,<sup>[https://web.archive.org/web/20160907055406/http://alt-usage-english.org/excerpts/fxwhydow.html]</sup> in Mark Israel, the {{monospace|alt.usage.english}} FAQ.</ref> In the UK, however, ''foot'' is colloquially used as a plural in all contexts for the unit of measure, even where such usage would not be natural in other varieties of English.
** It is sometimes abbreviated '''[[']]''', such as in tables, lists or drawings.

